// BT-3163: BT3163WhileLoopInTryActor — pins the finding that a `whileTrue:`
// loop as an `ensure:` try body's LAST statement compiles cleanly, even
// with an earlier field mutation in the same try body forcing the inlined
// (non-closure) try shape that made BT-3161's two flavors fail. Every
// non-exhaustive boolean `case` `while_loops.rs` generates lives inside a
// `letrec`-bound loop `fun`'s own body, entered via `apply` — a genuinely
// separate BEAM function from the `try`'s own function, structurally unable
// to trip erlc's `ambiguous_catch_try_state` beam_validator bug. See
// `control_flow/while_loops.rs`'s module doc comment (BT-3163) for the full
// analysis.

Actor subclass: BT3163WhileLoopInTryActor
  state: count = 0

  // The loop runs on a local of the try body: a loop there that writes the
  // parameter (an outer local) loses the write today, which ADR 0131 Phase 0
  // rejects (BT-3753).
  runUnsafe: startFlag =>
    [
      self.count := self.count + 1
      flag := startFlag
      [flag] whileTrue: [flag := false]
    ] ensure: [nil]

  getCount => self.count
